-- title:
--   Simultaneous dilatation along a descending chain of closed strata
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a domain), $K$ a field which is an $R$-algebra and a fraction field of $R$, and let $f\colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism of schemes that is locally of finite type. Let $t \in \mathbb{N}$ and let $Y \colon \mathbb{N} \to \mathcal{P}(X)$ be a family of subsets with each $Y_i$ closed, $Y_{i+1} \subseteq Y_i$ for all $i$, $Y_t = \emptyset$, and $f(y)$ equal to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ for every $y \in Y_0$. The assertion is the existence of a scheme $X_1$ and a morphism $v \colon X_1 \to X$ such that: $v$ is separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact; the canonical map $X_1 \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} K \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} K$ induced by $v$ and the identities of $\operatorname{Spec} K$ (the base change being along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to K$) is an isomorphism; the restriction of $v$ over the open complement of $Y_0$ is an isomorphism; for every discrete valuation ring $R'$ that is an $R$-algebra with $\mathfrak{m}_R R' = \mathfrak{m}_{R'}$, every morphism $x \colon \operatorname{Spec} R' \to X$ with $x \circ{}$(nothing) — precisely, every $x$ with $f \circ x$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to R'$ — admits a unique $x_1 \colon \operatorname{Spec} R' \to X_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ (i.e. with $(v \circ x_1)$ composed with $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $R \to R'$) such that $x_1$ followed by $v$ is $x$; and, finally, a chart description: for every $i < t$, every affine open $U \subseteq X$ disjoint from $Y_{i+1}$ and every $\pi \in R$ generating $\mathfrak{m}_R$, there are an open $W \subseteq X_1$ and an isomorphism $e$ of $W$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the affine dilatation ring [`AffineDilatation.Ring`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20) $I\,a$ — the $A$-subalgebra of `Localization.Away` $a$ generated by `gen` $I\,a$, where $A = \Gamma(X,U)$, $I$ is the vanishing ideal of the set of primes of $A$ corresponding to the points of $U$ lying in $Y_i$, and $a$ is the image of $\pi$ in $A$ under $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R) \to \Gamma(X,X) \to \Gamma(X,U)$ — such that the inclusion of $W$ followed by $v$ equals $e$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $A \to$ [`AffineDilatation.Ring`](def/RingTheory_AffineDilatation.html#L20) $I\,a$ followed by the canonical $\operatorname{Spec} A \to X$, and such that for every $R'$ as above and every $x_1 \colon \operatorname{Spec} R' \to X_1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ whose composite with $v$ sends the closed point of $R'$ into $Y_i \cap U$, the point $x_1(\text{closed point})$ lies in $W$.
--
--   This is the simultaneous dilatation construction of Bosch–Lütkebohmert–Raynaud (Néron Models, 3.2 and the proof of 3.4, Theorem 2): the scheme $X_1$ is obtained by gluing the open complement of $Y_0$ with the dilatations of the strata $Y_i \setminus Y_{i+1}$ of the special fibre, and it has the same $R'$-points as $X$ for unramified extensions $R'/R$ of discrete valuation rings. It feeds the smoothening process, being used by [`NeronModelInfra.exists_hom_isIso_smoothnessDefect_add_one_le_of_smooth_pullback_snd`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.exists_hom_isIso_smoothnessDefect_add_one_le_of_smooth_pullback_snd); the single-centre case is [`NeronModelInfra.exists_isAffineHom_isIso_morphismRestrict_iso_affineDilatation_of_isClosed`](thm.html#NeronModelInfra.exists_isAffineHom_isIso_morphismRestrict_iso_affineDilatation_of_isClosed).
